# omi.oss.release.env — the release of THIS self-hosted stack (ADR-0054).
#
# One number describing the whole thing: it tags the five images we build (backend, whisper, parakeet,
# diarizer, nllb) and, together with omi.oss.release.pins (what we borrow — ADR-0055), it is the bill of
# materials of a release. SemVer, kept in step with the Helm chart's appVersion, which is a PROJECTION of
# this value: a CI check fails if the two drift.
#
# Compose reads this through the long form of `include:` in each entry file, next to the pins:
#
#   include:
#     - path: compose.base.yaml
#       env_file:
#         - omi.oss.release.env
#         - omi.oss.release.pins
#
# The variable is spelled OMI_OSS_RELEASE because dots are not valid in compose interpolation; the dotted
# form omi.oss.release is the same concept as an OCI image label and a Kubernetes object label.
#
# Bumping it: change the line, align Chart.yaml (version + appVersion), rebuild. The build tags each image
# with this release AND with :latest — :latest is a DEV alias only (Kind loads it with `kind load`), never
# a production reference; the chart's prod/k0s overlays are not allowed to use it.
#
# This file is source, not operator configuration: it is committed (the .gitignore of this directory
# re-includes it against the repo-wide *.env rule) and it must stay tracked.
OMI_OSS_RELEASE=0.2.0
